{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Marker Packaging.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Marker Packaging.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"jpeg marker packaging jpeg marker packaging","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Marker Packaging.md","fileName":"JPEG Marker Packaging.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"JPEG Marker Packaging","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 00:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Image Metadata and JPEG Signatures]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Image Metadata and JPEG Signatures","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Marker Packaging.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Marker Packaging.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"jpeg marker packaging jpeg marker packaging","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Marker Packaging.md","fileName":"JPEG Marker Packaging.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"JPEG Marker Packaging","heading":"JPEG Marker Packaging","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"JPEG marker packaging is the arrangement of segments that identify image parameters, quantization and coding tables, metadata, scan data, and the file's beginning and end. The standard permits flexibility, so cameras and editing applications often emit recognizable marker orders and payload conventions.\n\nWhen software opens and resaves a photograph, it may reconstruct this packaging even if the visible pixels change little. Comparing the structure with reference files can therefore reveal an unexpected encoder, though firmware versions and export options can produce legitimate variation.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Image Metadata and JPEG Signatures","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Marker Packaging.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/JPE